===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|knobelouch}}, with dissimilation from {{m|gmh|klobelouch}} from {{inh|de|goh|chlobalouh|lit=[[clove]]-[[leek]]}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*klobulauk}}; from now {{m|de|klieben|t=cleave}} and {{m|de|Lauch|t=leek}}. The dissimilated ''kl-'' was adapted to the large group of terms for thick objects beginning with ''kn-'' (cf. {{m|de|Knopf}}, {{m|de|Knoten}}, {{m|de|Knolle}}, etc.). The same in {{cog|nl|knoflook}}.

